1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Welcome to the FinData UPI Fraud Intelligence Platform demo for the TransOrg AgentIQ Datathon Track 1.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,500
In this challenge, we were given messy UPI, KYC, merchant, and chargeback datasets containing inconsistent identifiers, formats, duplicates, and broken relationships.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:27,500
Instead of discarding records or running black-box models on dirty data, we engineered an end-to-end forensic pipeline.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,500
It rescues data, surfaces fraud syndicates, and powers conversational graph intelligence.

5
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:45,500
In the Data Rescue and Forensic Audit Center, you can see our entity resolution engine in action.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:53,500
We ingested 36,400 raw KYC records and unified them into 28,920 golden customer profiles.

7
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:01,500
We reconciled 6,210 raw merchant records down to 4,343 authoritative golden merchants.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
20,400 raw logs were cleaned into 20,000 trusted transactions, and 2,884 raw chargebacks yielded 2,800 trusted chargebacks.

9
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:18,500
Crucially, we preserved every single raw record with forensic audit tags rather than blindly deleting them.

10
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:28,500
Here is merchant MCH7912, where 6 conflicting raw rows were resolved with a complete before-and-after audit trail.

11
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:34,500
Next, we move to the Executive Dashboard.

12
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:45,500
Across Q1 2026, the platform processed INR 249.77M across 20,000 transactions, with 2,800 chargebacks representing a 14% dispute rate.

13
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:52,500
Our category risk matrix immediately spotlights risk concentrations across the payment ecosystem.

14
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:02,500
Apparel leads the platform with a 30.34% chargeback-to-transaction ratio, followed by Miscellaneous Retail at 18.87%.

15
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:10,500
Real-time telemetry tracks hourly fraud velocity, settlement latency spikes, and payment mode volume distributions.

16
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:19,500
In the Merchant Risk Intelligence Center, risk analysts can filter and prioritize high-risk merchants across categories.

17
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:27,500
Let us inspect Date Plc, merchant MCH4790, which carries a critical risk score of 95 out of 100.

18
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:36,500
The platform connects transactions to customer chargebacks, exposing a 90% dispute concentration and abnormal velocity.

19
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:43,500
Automated investigation priority scoring allows risk teams to take proactive mitigation action.

20
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:51,500
Now, we explore the Fraud Ring Intelligence Center.

21
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:58,500
Traditional rule engines evaluate transactions in isolation, missing coordinated collusive rings.

22
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:06,500
Our platform constructs multi-hop graph topologies linking customers, transactions, merchants, and chargebacks.

23
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:13,500
Look at Ring Settle 001, a shared settlement syndicate with a maximum risk score of 100.

24
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:21,500
By inspecting the graph, we uncover multiple unrelated merchant storefronts funneling illicit proceeds into a single shared bank account.

25
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
The system flags this multi-merchant laundering syndicate and maps every connected entity.

26
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:33,500
Moving to the Customer and Identity Risk Center, we identify synthetic identity clusters.

27
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,500
Customer USR62254, Oni Subramanian, carries a 90 risk score.

28
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:48,000
The engine flags shared PAN numbers across multiple phone numbers, high chargeback filing rates, and identity anomalies.

29
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:57,500
With one click, the platform generates a regulatory-compliant FIU-IND Suspicious Transaction Report dossier for law enforcement submission.

30
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:03,500
Now, let us open the Agentic AI Assistant.

31
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:09,500
The agent connects conversational natural language to our deterministic graph engine.

32
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:17,000
We ask: Which merchant category has the highest chargeback-to-transaction ratio this quarter?

33
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:25,500
The agent computes the grounded result directly on trusted data: Apparel at 30.34% with 44 chargebacks on 145 transactions, and renders an interactive chart.

34
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Next, we ask: Why is it important?

35
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:38,000
The agent provides the strategic business explanation: Apparel exceeds the 1.0% NPCI regulatory threshold by 30 times.

36
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:45,500
It suffers from high-liquidity stolen card testing and requires immediate rolling reserve protection.

37
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:52,500
Security and reliability are built into every layer.

38
00:04:53,000 --> 00:05:00,000
When we ask an out-of-domain query like: Who is the Prime Minister of India?, the agent immediately triggers application-level domain guardrails and refuses.

39
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:08,000
The platform enforces multi-tier prompt injection protection, an OpenRouter multi-model cascade with automatic free-tier fallback.

40
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:14,000
And a deterministic mathematical engine that eliminates hallucinations.

41
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:24,500
To conclude: We transformed unreliable payment data into an auditable fraud intelligence system that does not just report risk, it helps investigators find and understand it.

42
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,500
Thank you.
